a:Tbec,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How many total rakats are in all 5 daily prayers combined (namaz ki rakat)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Counting all Fard, Sunnah, Nafl, and Witr prayers, the full routine consists of 48 rakats (17 Fard, 12 Sunnah Mu’akkadah, 8 Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah, 6 Nafl, 3 Witr, and 2 Nafl). The bare obligatory requirement is 17 Fard rakats plus Witr."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the exact breakdown for Zuhar namaz rakat and Asr namaz rakat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Zuhar namaz rakat consists of 12 rakats in total: 4 Sunnah Mu’akkadah, 4 Fard, 2 Sunnah Mu’akkadah, and 2 Nafl. Asr namaz rakat consists of 8 rakats in total: 4 Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah followed by 4 Fard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are Namaz Ke Faraiz (the essential obligations of prayer)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In classical Islamic Fiqh, Namaz Ke Faraiz comprise 13 mandatory elements: 6 pre-conditions before prayer (Taharah, Satr-e-Awrah, Istiqbal-e-Qibla, Waqt, Niyyah, Takbeer-e-Tahrimah) and 7 internal pillars (Qiyam, Qira’at, Ruku, Sujood, Qa’dah Akhirah, Khurooj bi-San’ihi, and Tuma’ninah). Omitting any Fard invalidates the prayer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is Tasbeeh Namaz (Salat al-Tasbeeh) performed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tasbeeh Namaz consists of 4 rakats with 300 repetitions of the third Kalimah (\"Subhanallahi wal-hamdulillahi wa la ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar\"): 15 times after Sana, 10 after Surah, 10 in Ruku, 10 in Qawmah, 10 in first Sajdah, 10 in Jalsah, and 10 in second Sajdah (75 per rakat x 4 = 300)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the procedure for Namaz Janaza and the Janaza Namaz Dua?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Namaz Janaza is performed standing with 4 Takbeers (no Ruku or Sujood): 1st Takbeer followed by Sana; 2nd Takbeer followed by Durood Ibrahim; 3rd Takbeer followed by the authentic Janaza Namaz Dua (\"Allahumma ighfir li hayyina wa mayyitina...\"); and 4th Takbeer followed by Salam to right and left."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Beter namaz porar niyom (rules for Witr prayer)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Bengali tradition according to the Hanafi school (Beter namaz porar niyom), Witr consists of 3 continuous rakats. In the 3rd rakat, after reciting Surah Al-Fatiha and a surah, raise hands saying Allahu Akbar, fold hands again, and recite Dua-e-Qunoot before bowing into Ruku."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the rules regarding Namaz Chadar and Namaz e Ghufayla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Namaz Chadar refers to the full-body loose covering worn by Muslim sisters ensuring that only the face, hands to wrists, and feet are visible throughout prayer. Namaz e Ghufayla is a 2-rakat voluntary prayer recommended between Maghrib and Isha in Ja’fari tradition with recitation of Surah Al-Anbiya (21:87-88) and Surah Al-An’am (6:59)."}}]}7:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-12 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Namaz Rakats Guide\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/rakats\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$a"}}],"$Lb"]}],null,"$Lc"]}]
